<spell-notebook "advertisement theming">
	<header level="1">
		Advertisement
		<header>An ad displays third-party promotional content.</>
	</>
	<advertisement-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-ad-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region,
			`:root`), or on the ad's box through `::part(ad)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the
			sheet reads each through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. The unit sizes are fixed
			by the IAB, so they aren't tokens. Never set the `--_ui-ad-*` names: they're the sheet's private
			plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			:root {
			  --ui-ad-margin: 2em 0;
			  --ui-ad-test-background: var(--ui-surface-muted);
			  --ui-ad-test-color: var(--ui-text-muted);
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-ad" playground>
				<ui-ad unit="medium rectangle" test="Medium rectangle"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Every theme of the set (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) leaves ads their own look, and changes the
			page around them.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
